# Design

The studio is a dashboard on `#0B0A1A`. Two soft radial gradients, violet `#5B3FD6` and blue `#2B4FD8`, sit at low opacity, with a very subtle noise texture. Glass is `rgba(255,255,255,0.06)`, border `rgba(255,255,255,0.12)`, a 1px top highlight `rgba(255,255,255,0.18)`, blur 20px, saturate 140%. Use glass on at most six surfaces at once: the sidebar, the composer, the brief, the reasoning, the layers, and the tour popover.

Ink `#F4F2FF` is primary text. Secondary `#B8B3D9`. Muted `#8A84B3`. All text meets 4.5 to 1. On the accent `#8B6CFF`, text is `#0B0A1A`. The accent is for primary actions and the focus ring, with a soft glow on hover only. Success `#4FD1C5`, warning `#F5B971`, error `#FF8A8A`.

Geist Sans is the interface. Geist Mono is for BPM, key, seeds, and file names. The greeting is 56px semibold at 1440px and wider, 44px below that, with a subtle vertical gradient from `#F4F2FF` to `#C9C2FF`. Section titles are 15px semibold. Body is 15px. Secondary copy is 13px. Tempo and key are 28px semibold. Spacing stays on an 8px grid.

Lane hues are Drums `#FF6B57`, Chords `#F5C451`, Bass `#3FD0A8`, Melody `#6C8CFF`, and Texture `#B07CFF`. They fill that layer's card and chip. Ink on a lane is `#0B0A1A`. Full mix has no sixth hue.

Radius is 24px for large cards, 16px for inner cards, 12px for inputs, and full round for chips and pills. Sentence case. No all caps.

Focus is a 2px accent outline, offset 2px. Motion is the greeting leaving, messages arriving, brief rows filling, and layer cards appearing. Reduced motion makes those instant.

At 1440×900 the sidebar is 240px and the rail is 320px. Canvas content sits in a centred column at most 760px wide. The sidebar names Vision Studio, lists Song idea, and shows Song analyser and Song edits with a Soon pill when those flags are off. Recent ideas, the latest 20, come from localStorage and can be restored, renamed, or deleted. Help and the session pill sit at the bottom. Before any input the canvas centres the greeting, the composer, the quick start chips, and three how-it-works cards, and the rail shows Getting started plus Layers. After the first turn, the canvas is a thread, the composer stays docked, and the rail shows the brief, the trace, and Build. After Build, layer cards sit in the thread and a player offers Play together and Export to Logic. The home view fits at 1280×800 and 1440×900 without page scrolling.

Under 1200px the rail is a tabbed panel above the composer. Under 768px the sidebar is a drawer. Record, solo and mute, full mix, the styleguide link, the demo chip, and the Soon items follow `apps/web/src/features.ts`. Layer cards and the player load lazily.
